@startuml
title Generate once, load the same JSON
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor User
participant CLI
participant GenerateProfile as Generate
participant "KernelProfileLoader /\nProcIomemProfileLoader" as Source
participant SubprocessRunner as Runner
participant JsonProfileWriter as Writer
database "profile.json" as File
participant "Analysis caller" as Caller
participant JsonProfileLoader as Loader

User -> CLI: generate kernel profile to profile.json
CLI -> Generate: run()
Generate -> Source: load()
Source -> Runner: run(CommandSpec for /proc/iomem)
Runner --> Source: command output
Source -> Source: parse observed ranges and collection diagnostics
Source --> Generate: PlatformProfile
Generate -> Writer: write(profile, output_path)
Writer -> File: serialize existing producer fields
Generate --> CLI: complete
CLI --> User: exit status

== Later, through the Python analysis API ==
Caller -> Loader: load(ProfileSelection(path))
Loader -> File: read UTF-8 JSON
File --> Loader: original JSON object
Loader -> Loader: validate JSON; freeze objects and arrays
Loader --> Caller: AnalysisProfile(filename, data)
note over Caller, Loader
  No path -> empty default.
  Invalid explicit input -> ProfileLoadError.
  No conversion or automatic security classification.
end note
@enduml
